# Atom framework state
#
# events.jsonl is a machine-generated append-only log -- genuinely not source.
#
# .atom/state.json is deliberately NOT ignored (B173). It records project
# configuration and human approvals, which are project history. Ignoring it is
# what made `atom status` report "Phase: unknown" in this very repository: the
# file Atom treated as its sole source of truth never survived a clone. What is
# left in it now cannot be derived from the filesystem, so it has to be kept.
.atom/events.jsonl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Go
*.exe
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch space for measurement logs and workflow artifacts.
.temp/

# Blast-radius experiment working data.
#
# This measurement runs against a private repository, so everything the driver
# produces is saturated with that repo's internal file paths, commit hashes and
# name -- 761 path references at last count, plus 72 raw agent replies whose whole
# purpose is to name real files in it. None of that can be published.
#
# The brief and the driver are worth publishing once the repo-specific parts are
# replaced with placeholders. Until that work is done the whole tree stays local,
# because a leak into git history cannot be taken back.
poc/blast-radius/
specs/blast-radius/
